<title>USA: Bear Stearns says ex-NatWest trader on leave.</title>
<headline>Bear Stearns says ex-NatWest trader on leave.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bear Stearns Cos Inc on Tuesday said Kyriacos Papouis, a former National Westminster Bank Plc options trader now employed by Bear Stearns, was on leave from the firm.</p>
<p>Papouis is at the center of a NatWest internal probe of $81 million in options losses involving mispricing of interest rate options transactions, banking sources said.</p>
<p>A Bear Stearns spokeswoman declined to offer any additional details, saying only, &quot;He's currently on leave, pending further information.&quot;</p>
<p>((-- Wall Street desk, 212-859-1730))</p>
